#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0306 expect=noViolation domain=DM
#note "PLAN-scalar-date-extremes (T2 round-2 review M3): Subject 001 has an own EX row (EXSTDTC 2020-01-05, EXENDTC blank) and is in two pools: P1 with two EX rows (2020-01-01, blank) and (2020-01-10, blank), P2 with one (2020-01-03, blank); RFXENDTC 2020-01-10. Every EXENDTC is blank, so the latest EXENDTC is undeterminable on every part and the EXENDTC conjunct fires on the missing answer (D34a); the EXSTDTC fallback decides: the per-pool latest EXSTDTC is P1 2020-01-10 and P2 2020-01-03, the outer POOLDEF extreme takes the later pool (2020-01-10), and latest_date(own 2020-01-05, pool 2020-01-10) = 2020-01-10 = RFXENDTC -> silent. Pins the EXSTDTC path's three directions: an inner min_date (P1 2020-01-01), an outer min_date (P2 2020-01-03) or earliest_date for $last_exstdtc (2020-01-05) would each report the row."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFXENDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of Last Study Treatment"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 2020-01-10
---
dataset EX class=INTERVENTIONS label="Exposure"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col POOLID  type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col EXSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col EXTRT   type=Char label="Name of Treatment"
col EXSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Treatment"
col EXENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Treatment"
---
S1 | EX | 001 |  | 1 | DRUG A | 2020-01-05 |
S1 | EX |  | P1 | 2 | DRUG A | 2020-01-01 |
S1 | EX |  | P1 | 3 | DRUG A | 2020-01-10 |
S1 | EX |  | P2 | 4 | DRUG A | 2020-01-03 |
---
dataset POOLDEF label="Pool Definition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col POOLID  type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
S1 | P1 | 001
S1 | P2 | 001
---
